From 391d633da717e6781c9c7839d31d285c7a2f9ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 4 <phase4@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 06:53:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] RISC-V: assemble WCH custom 32-bit instructions

The official WCH 12.2 assembler accepts the four observed custom forms from rv32i and enforces the observed funct5 operand range and constant-only constraint. Add ordinary opcode-table entries plus the funct5 operand class in the validator, the parser and the printer. The third GPR operand these forms take already exists upstream in the validator and the parser; only the disassembler was missing its printing case.

WCH 12.2 behavior evidence: tmp/phase4-evidence/s3-custom32-official/ and tmp/phase4-evidence/s3-custom32-final/. Encoding reference: ref/wch-isa-research/isa/custom/wch-custom-isa-reference.md section 5, whose mcpy field table is quoted from CH32V407RM V1.1 section 9.2.1.4.
---
 gas/config/tc-riscv.c                       | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32-fail.d |  2 ++
 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32-fail.l |  7 +++++++
 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32-fail.s |  3 +++
 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32.d      | 13 +++++++++++++
 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32.s      |  5 +++++
 include/opcode/riscv-opc.h                  | 12 ++++++++++++
 include/opcode/riscv.h                      |  2 ++
 opcodes/riscv-dis.c                         | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 opcodes/riscv-opc.c                         |  4 ++++
 10 files changed, 83 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32-fail.d
 create mode 100644 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32-fail.l
 create mode 100644 gas/testsuite/gas/riscv/wch-custom32-fail.s
